# Fiberplane local issue tracking
.fp/
FP_CLAUDE.md

# pkgdown site (generated). _pkgdown.yml sets no `destination:`, so a local
# build_site() writes the whole site here. Nothing needs it in git: the `pages`
# job in .gitlab-ci.yml rebuilds the site in CI and hands the result to GitLab
# Pages as a `public/` artifact, so no branch ever carries it (the GitHub
# workflow this replaced pushed it to a gh-pages branch, which is why that
# branch existed).
# .Rbuildignore already keeps it out of the tarball (^docs$, ^docs/.*); this
# closes the other half, so a site build cannot be committed wholesale.
/docs/

# GitLab Pages artifact directory, produced by `mv docs public` in CI and by
# anyone reproducing the pages job locally.
/public/
